Frequency/Likelihood of Future Occurrence
Figure 4.5 indicates that drought occurs approximately every ten years in Laramie County.
Figure 4.5 indicates that the planning area spent 10-15% of the 100 year span from 1895 to 1995
in severe or extreme drought.  This is consistent with the data in Table 4.5, which suggests that
severe multi-year droughts have occurred roughly every ten years since the mid-20th century.  An
occurrence interval of roughly once every ten years corresponds to a likely frequency of
occurrence.
